; [0.8.1-RT14] (#954), work #955: the six ATTDEFs of autocad-attributi, one per mode, each
; with AFLAGS 0 and the mode turned on by the question of -ATTDEF, in the order and with the
; answers of the history (card PT14, points 1-2 and "Le domande del testo"; docs/adr/0056,
; point 2). Constant asks the value and no prompt; prompts and defaults keep their spaces.
; AFLAGS takes the modes used: 0, 1, 2, 4, 8, 16 as in the history. TENSIONE picks ARIAL with
; Style: the repeated line says "ARIAL" and ARIAL becomes current (decision on #954, point
; 4); the history then sets TEXTSTYLE back to Standard, here with -STYLE Standard. SIGLA is
; justified MC (Specify middle point of text:) and rotated by 10 degrees.
; Source: Matleyx78/dxf-test-file, commit 2aafbb1fa17abc67fdf2ff7de26a34b70e79b736
; (CC0-1.0): autocad-attributi.scr and autocad-attributi.txt (AutoCAD 2021, Italian,
; translated as docs/adr/0056, point 2, and card PT14). The ARIAL style is made with -STYLE
; and the prompts of style/cambia-esistente and text/stile-altezza-fissa; its record takes
; handle 257, so the ATTDEFs start at 258.
; Not visible, chosen as the simplest: an ATTDEF justified other than Left keeps the given
; point both as position and alignment-point (the drawing uses only the alignment point,
; docs/adr/0022, point 2).
; ~box (docs/adr/0022): LiberationSans-Regular.ttf of resources/fonts, read with a small
; reader of its head, hhea, OS/2, cmap and hmtx tables: cap height 1409, ascent 1854,
; descent -434, summed advances; an ATTDEF shows its tag. arial.ttf is Liberation Sans.
